<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3cb5abea515e8416431740d1bb4b4c6cfeb224cf" commit="294ce9604163dcf45aa4deb321fbb1b21abfb92b" commit_message="chroot_version_hooks.d: make `sudo -v` don't ask for password  Even though we mark the user as NOPASSWD, if any other rules match them, the `sudo -v` command ends up prompting for a password.  Add a rule disabling that in case rules happen to trigger it.  BUG=chromium:762445 TEST=cros_sdk --nousepkg --replace --enter --nouse-image; sudo -v  Change-Id: I3cb5abea515e8416431740d1bb4b4c6cfeb224cf Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/652206 Commit-Ready: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="652206" owner_email="stimim@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/crosutils" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/crosutils" ref="refs/changes/06/652206/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I730a85df5f783d001b96d5608ed621aafa7b7ad4" commit="7109b0ee3b917fb331cc1f6c9fadb66571214b72" commit_message="login: fix flag for background blur.  Flag changed from &quot;--enable-background-blur&quot; to &quot;--enable-feature=EnableBackgroundBlur&quot;.  BUG=chromium:749145 TEST=Deploy login_manager to Eve and check that command line include flag is used.  Change-Id: I730a85df5f783d001b96d5608ed621aafa7b7ad4 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/653917 Commit-Ready: David Reveman &lt;reveman@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: David Reveman &lt;reveman@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="653917" owner_email="reveman@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/17/653917/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I38fa7f5a8549badb778c12336779e8f713c12d67" commit="e65308b340b7268f8bc48698200445c7a80960b7" commit_message="create softlink from usb_updater to gsctool and use the new name  As part of the gradual transition of renaming usb_updater into gsctool let's first create a softlink to have the new name point to the old one, and update various scripts using this utility name to use the new name.  BRANCH=none BUG=b:65415950 TEST=built chrome OS images for Eve and Bob, installed them and      observed that the Cr50 got updated at the postinstall phase.      Also, fall back the Eve Cr50 image and reboot the device, observe      the new image installed at startup.  Change-Id: I38fa7f5a8549badb778c12336779e8f713c12d67 Signed-off-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/654062 Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="654062" owner_email="vbendeb@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/62/654062/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie667f0dbf0be4742125d4d2f56d9f75abf5b389a" commit="eb8713fac2410eea60c326a1d1fbddf69ba6d004" commit_message="finalize_bundle: guide user to BUNDLE.md on invalid MANIFEST.yaml  The format of MANIFEST.yaml has benn changed a lot recently.  Not all partners are aware of that.  If one tries to copy paste an old manifest and run finalize_bundle, the error message is not clear (e.g. it will complain about '!glob').  We should guide them to read BUNDLE.md, so they will know the format has been changed.  BUG=None TEST=None  Change-Id: Ie667f0dbf0be4742125d4d2f56d9f75abf5b389a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/651989 Commit-Ready: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Youcheng Syu &lt;youcheng@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="651989" owner_email="stimim@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/89/651989/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I773f743eed4ee7d7e28f64d259313ea13644042f" commit="e9ea4e1ff8c63cba673bb30b258861a3f5590868" commit_message="test_list_checker: a static test list checker  tools/test_list_checker.py helps you check if your test list is valid statically.  This script can be run on device or in chroot.  If you run it on device (DUT), you don't need to add `--board` argument.  When the script is run in chroot, use `--board` argument to specify the board you are working on.  Because board overlay might create their own pytests (or override existing pytests).  We use `make overlay-&lt;board&gt;` to create a directory containing both files from factory repo and board overlay.  So we can check the pytest arguments against the correct pytest files.  BUG=b:64885065 TEST=tools/test_list_checker.py --board soraka main TEST=override message/message.py in soraka overlay, run      `tools/test_list_checker.py --board soraka main`  Change-Id: I773f743eed4ee7d7e28f64d259313ea13644042f Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/652046 Commit-Ready: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="652046" owner_email="stimim@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/46/652046/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie5e701b2fc9a97f612f0acf9fefc2e5dd2066d2c" commit="073180407a21f468147f1ff56d9f22239ec9b73a" commit_message="configs: Rename config VBT_DATA to INTEL_GMA_VBT_DATA  Coreboot change 9b7be60 (UPSTREAM: Kconfig: Move and rename ADD_VBT_DATA_FILE) renamed config VBT_DATA to INTEL_GMA_VBT_DATA. However, configs for different mainboards were not updated to reflect this change. Because of this, on soraka/poppy, display did not work in firmware and OS got stuck on ChromeOS logo.  This change updates all mainboards to use updated config.  BUG=b:65431045 BRANCH=None TEST=Verified that display works in firmware and OS on soraka.  Change-Id: Ie5e701b2fc9a97f612f0acf9fefc2e5dd2066d2c Signed-off-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/654300 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="654300" owner_email="furquan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/00/654300/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic5771895a214a9f1aa9bd289eef576f52adf973f" commit="656c87d2391c751c389d53e77b28a424885563b7" commit_message="cleanup: Remove jtag_pre_init()  Use our newly-created chip_pre_init() for doing JTAG initialization.  BUG=chromium:747629 BRANCH=None TEST=`make buildall -j`  Signed-off-by: Shawn Nematbakhsh &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: Ic5771895a214a9f1aa9bd289eef576f52adf973f Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/629676 Commit-Ready: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="629676" owner_email="shawnn@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/76/629676/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2f05c527bd99f9dfa47861c1d2690b0cc4132819" commit="695519ad1a98859398411beed9c5bd270a9f834d" commit_message="Refactoring and minor fixes for more code-reuse.  Made the PausePlay and ResolutionSwitching tests use the test_webrtc_peer_connection module to avoid repeating test boilerplate.  Added a verification method to loopback-peerconnection.js and use that method to verify the streams are OK instead of custom logic per test. This method accepts some bad video resolution reports, since the SwitchResolution test incorrectly fails now in the lab since occasionally resolutions are reported as 0x0.  Minor fixes in ResolutionSwitching and PausePlay javascripts to fix issues brought up in reviews of the MainFeedSwitching test.  Removed the FeedTable from the pauseplay tests. There is no reason to arrenge the feeds in a table, it just adds complexity.  Other minor changes.  BUG=chromium:760676 TEST=Ran all affected tests against local DUT  Change-Id: I2f05c527bd99f9dfa47861c1d2690b0cc4132819 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/653957 Commit-Ready: Kristoffer Erlandsson &lt;kerl@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Kristoffer Erlandsson &lt;kerl@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Denis Tosic &lt;dtosic@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="653957" owner_email="kerl@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/57/653957/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I75e2cfc39f22483d9e9b32c5f8b887dbafc37108" commit="d74992710c5e3249789b88354eea7760e6e1857c" commit_message="g: restore DATA PID after USB suspend/resume  In USB FS on a bulk/interrupt endpoint, the transactions normally toggles between DATA0 and DATA1 PIDs. After a USB suspend/resume cycle, we need to restart from the PID we were at before suspend. In our current code, when going to deep-sleep during USB suspend, we are re-initializing everything when the MCU restarts at each resume. So we set implicitly the PID to DATA0. The USB Hardware IP just silently discards the packet when the PID of an incoming OUT packet is not matching the expectation in the endpoint register.  In order to preserve DATA PIDS, record the state of the PID toggling on each endpoint when going to deep-sleep and restore it during the USB initialization.  Signed-off-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt;  BRANCH=none BUG=b:38160821 TEST=manual, plug a HG proto2 on a Linux host machine and enable 'auto-suspend' for this USB device. Let it go to sleep and wake-it up by sending a U2FHID request. Repeat the process several times and see that the key answers every time (while it was failing after the second cycle before).  Change-Id: I75e2cfc39f22483d9e9b32c5f8b887dbafc37108 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/655238 Commit-Ready: Marius Schilder &lt;mschilder@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Marius Schilder &lt;mschilder@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="655238" owner_email="vpalatin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/38/655238/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id5c65badced1b1b06ec4da549399e0137d287794" commit="59e0dc3bb5406b812984e1a04f28475ccf2788b6" commit_message="Adjust DetermineAndroidBranch to support alternate build targets  BUG=None TEST=./cbuildbot_run_unittest  Change-Id: Id5c65badced1b1b06ec4da549399e0137d287794 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/653590 Commit-Ready: Ben Lin &lt;linben@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Bernie Tho